    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter the 2026-07-07 slate with a lineup anchored by three high-upside plays exceeding the 78-point threshold. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13) sits atop our efficiency rankings; he benefits from a massive park boost (+16%) and a favorable matchup against Baz, but he carries a 45% rain risk warning that requires monitoring. **Trea Turner** (79.76) and **Kyle Schwarber** (78.41) are also locked into elite tiers, both capitalizing on a juicy matchup against the struggling Abbott, A. With **Schwarber** enjoying an extra boost from a +19% SP skill advantage and **Turner** providing essential stolen base upside, these three represent the core offensive engine for today\u2019s campaign.\n\nThe optimization process relied heavily on dynamic platoon edges to navigate a crowded roster. **Colt Keith** (69.48) remains a must-start, as his +7% platoon advantage and +8% order bump in the two-hole make him a high-floor producer against Ginn. Meanwhile, **Caleb Durbin** (62.58) makes the cut over other utility options; his ability to exploit the +19% SP skill advantage against Schultz outweighs the minor negative adjustment for the opposing catcher\u2019s hold percentage. On the bench, **Nelson Velazquez** (55.26) was the most difficult exclusion. Despite an elite xwOBA (0.418) and a solid platoon edge, **Velazquez** ultimately lost out to the superior overall efficiency of **Carson Benge** (55.45) and the strategic necessity of keeping **Christian Yelich** in the outfield rotation. While **Yordan Alvarez** (52.37) grades out lower than usual due to a difficult matchup against Alvarez, his elite 0.479 xwOBA provides the ceiling we need to offset the potential volatility of **Crow-Armstrong**'s weather-impacted start.",
